Bootstrap: docker
From: python:3

%labels
  MAINTAINER Daniel Dopp <danieldopp@uky.edu>
  VERSION 1.3

%post
  # Build directory structure for LCC
  mkdir /scratch
  mkdir /project
  mkdir /pscratch
  mkdir /share
  mkdir /opt/ohpc
  mkdir /mnt/gpfs2_16m
  mkdir /mnt/gpfs2_4m

  # Install git
  apt update
  apt install -y git

  # Upgrade pip
  pip3 install --upgrade pip

  # Clone the spectral analysis source from GitLab
  # TODO, figure out how to get this clone setup with ssh so an auto update can be written into the runscript
  git clone https://code.cs.uky.edu/seales-research/spectral-analysis.git

  # Switch to dev branch
  cd /spectral-analysis
  git checkout development

  # Install spectral analysis
  pipenv install -e .

  # Give read/write access in spectral-analysis (so it can later be edited using a persistent overlay)
  chmod --recursive a+rw /spectral-analysis

%runscript
  cd /spectral-analysis

  exec "$@"

%help
  This container provides an environment for running spectral-analysis package code.

  Building the container:
    - You will need to enter your https GitLab login information to initially clone the repository from source
    - Build as usual, for example: sudo singularity build spectral-analysis spectral-analysis.def

  Usage:
    - It is possible to use an overlay to allow one to pull changes to the dev branch only, or make local edits to spectral-analysis code:
      `dd if=/dev/zero of=spectral-analysis.overlay bs=1M count=500 && mkfs.ext3 spectral-analysis.overlay; singularity shell --overlay spectral-analysis.overlay spectral-analysis.sif
      This container is intended to be built once, and used with many checkouts of spectral-analysis code. Only when the dependencies change does the container need rebuilding.
